' purpose: bounded archive acquisition with network closure before independent readback
' covers: tooling/native-ingress/acquisition.mjs
' covers: tooling/native-ingress/acquisition.test.mjs
' context: _spec/_plans/ml-runtime-redesign.md section 24 owns goals and permissions.
' related: _spec/tooling/native-ingress/custody.puml owns the unchanged small fixture.
' scope: current ordinary DATA_ONLY helper; no online acquisition permission or Native authority.
' validation: parent reports 217 Node passes and scoped source reviews; offline rendering uses the approved local theme.
' rendering: retain house include; parent may substitute only the approved local theme in renderer input.
' readability: FK uses English syllable estimates with explicit engineering-token counts.
' FK: per-object note over ROOT,FILE = 10.8 (26 words, 47 syllables, 2 sentences).
' FK: close-uncertainty note over SOURCE,ERROR = 10.1 (28 words, 48 syllables, 2 sentences).
@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Ordinary archive acquisition — closure before readback, DATA_ONLY

actor "Operator-controlled caller" as CALLER <<host>>
participant "tooling/native-ingress/\nacquisition.mjs" as SOURCE <<app>>
participant "tooling/native-ingress/\ncustody.mjs" as CUSTODY <<app>>
participant "node:fs / node:crypto / process\nNode host runtime and timers" as HOST <<host>>
participant "node:https\nrequest / IncomingMessage" as NETWORK <<host>>
participant "toolchains.bootlin.com\nfixed HTTPS tarball origin" as HTTPS <<cloud>>
database "rootPath\nfresh directory" as ROOT <<db>>
database "descriptor.name\nfresh regular file" as FILE <<db>>
participant "CustodyError" as ERROR <<error>>

alt Fixed GNU comparison target
  CALLER ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : acquireGnu2026(rootPath)
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : acquireArtifact(rootPath, GNU2026_ARTIFACT)
else Operator-supplied descriptor, same origin policy
  CALLER ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : acquireArtifact(rootPath, input)
end
SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : first monotonic START; 119s work timer / 120s total
SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : validate absolute normalized non-root path
SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : createArtifactDescriptor(input); frozen independent snapshot
note right of SOURCE
Exact own data: name, url, byteLength, sha256
Object.prototype or null; no proxy/accessors
Safe basename .tar.xz, <=128 characters
Length 1..134217728; lowercase64-hex digest
URL = fixed Bootlin tarball prefix + name
end note

group Active outer try; any failure reaches descriptor finalization
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : check flags; capture effective UID; mkdirSync(0700, recursive:false)
  HOST ARROW_MAIN ROOT : fresh exclusive directory; EEXIST stops without inspection
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : opened(root): RDONLY | DIRECTORY | NOFOLLOW | NONBLOCK
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN CUSTODY : assertRoot(lstat, fstat, uid); retain rootBirth
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : opened(file): WRONLY | CREAT | EXCL | NOFOLLOW | NONBLOCK, 0600
  HOST ARROW_MAIN FILE : fresh regular file
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN CUSTODY : assertFileBirth(lstat, fstat, uid)
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : retain file birth; rootBinding() before transport
  note over ROOT, FILE
Each object retains its own device identity
because parent and file devices may differ.
Stable host paths remain required; checks cannot
protect ancestors against concurrent change.
  end note
  note over SOURCE, HOST
FD assigned before post-operation guard
Owned FDs <=2: root + writer OR reader
Positive path: three opens / three closes
No library unlink, rmdir, chmod or fsync
  end note

  group transfer(descriptor): one request, no retry or redirect
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN NETWORK : https.request(url, GET); attach error/close/response handlers
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN NETWORK : maxHeadersCount=33; request.end() once
    NETWORK ARROW_CLOUD HTTPS : verified TLS; agent:false; identity encoding; Connection:close
    HTTPS ARROW_CLOUD NETWORK : status / raw headers / streaming body
    NETWORK ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : receive(response); attach lifecycle/error handlers
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : assertHeaders(response, expected byteLength) before data handler
    note over SOURCE, NETWORK
status200; exactly one canonical length
<=32 raw pairs / <=16384 counted bytes
Absent encoding OR exactly one identity
No Transfer-Encoding / Content-Range
No auth, custom CA, proxy or fallback option
    end note
    loop data(chunk): <=32768 events, native Buffer length 1..1048576
      NETWORK ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : data event; ignore after failed/settled
      SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : intrinsic length/backing checks; reject proxy/SAB/excess bytes
      SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : bounded private copy; incremental incoming SHA-256
      SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : one full writeSync at explicit offset; partial count fails, no retry
      HOST ARROW_MAIN FILE : write private snapshot
    end
    NETWORK ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : end: complete===true; exact length and incoming SHA-256
    NETWORK ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : request close AND response close, either order
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : finish(): recheck response.complete before resolving transfer
  end

  alt transfer resolved with end, complete, both closes and incoming match
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN CUSTODY : assertFilePhase(lstat, fstat, uid, expected length)
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : birth SECURITY stable; snapshot written CONTENT; rootBinding()
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : close(writer): clear holder BEFORE single close attempt
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : opened(reader): RDONLY | NOFOLLOW | NONBLOCK
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN CUSTODY : assertFilePhase; full nine-field snapshot equals written
    loop exact positional slices <=65536 bytes
      SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : readSync; require full requested count
      HOST ARROW_MAIN FILE : independent readback
      SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : independent SHA-256; counts.readBytes += count
    end
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : one-byte EOF probe at expected length
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : require EOF and expected independent readback SHA-256
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN CUSTODY : assertFilePhase; written CONTENT unchanged
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : close(reader) once; rootBinding() via fstat/lstat
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : prepare ordinary-archive-acquisition-v1 / DATA_ONLY
  else transfer failure: absorbing state, no reader acquisition
    SOURCE ARROW_ERROR NETWORK : fail(): destroy request/response at most once each
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : cleanupEnd = min(total end, failure time + 1s)
    NETWORK ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : observe owned network close events before cleanupEnd
    opt destroy throws, close missing or observed too late
      SOURCE ARROW_ERROR ERROR : E_NETWORK_CLEANUP, with first failure as cause
    end
    SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : late body/end/error events inert; late first response destroyed
  end
end

group Unconditional descriptor finalization
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN HOST : finally: clear work timer; close remaining file/root holders once
  opt any filesystem close uncertain
    SOURCE ARROW_ERROR ERROR : E_CLOSE > E_NETWORK_CLEANUP > operation error; preserve cause chain
  end
end
note over SOURCE, ERROR
Close uncertainty prevents a success result
because descriptor disposition is no longer known.
The helper retains partial roots for inspection;
only the test removes its fresh owned paths.
end note

alt failure recorded
  SOURCE ARROW_ERROR CALLER : throw failure; no result
else all checks and closes succeeded
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : final total-deadline guard; freeze result and counts
  SOURCE ARROW_MAIN CALLER : contentMatched:true; expected/incoming/readback hashes; paths/devices
end
note right of CALLER
nativeAuthority/nativeQualified:false
provenanceVerified/pythonFreeSubsetVerified:false
installedUsability/rustReady/trainingReady:false
installationPerformed/immutabilityVerified:false
end note
note over SOURCE, HOST
fsCalls<=65533; closeAttempts<=3
clockReads<=200000; lifecycleEvents<=32
networkCalls<=4; no whole-payload array
Private chunk<=1MiB; read scratch64KiB
Cooperative guards; no hard native/RSS bound
end note
@enduml
